.TH INKMD 1 "2026-10-22" "inkmd 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inkmd \- render Markdown in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inkmd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inkmd
renders Markdown documents directly in the terminal and exits.
It supports CommonMark plus the GitHub Flavored Markdown extensions (tables,
task lists, strikethrough, footnotes, alerts, autolinks), front matter,
definition lists, math (converted to Unicode) and a safe subset of HTML.
.PP
Fenced code blocks are syntax highlighted.
On terminals that support them, images are drawn inline (Kitty graphics or
iTerm2 protocol) and headings are scaled by level (Kitty text sizing
protocol).
Every feature is detected at run time and falls back to plain text, so the
document always stays readable.
.PP
With no
.IR FILE ,
or when
.I FILE
is
.BR \- ,
standard input is read.
When standard output is not a terminal, plain text without escape sequences
is written, unless
.B \-\-color always
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Wrap at
.I N
columns (10\(en10000).
By default the terminal width is used, capped at 100 columns.
When standard output is not a terminal,
.B COLUMNS
or 80 is used.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " \fIWHEN\fR
Use colors and text styles:
.BR auto " (default), " always " or " never .
.B never
still allows bold and italic on a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Same as
.BR "\-\-color never" .
.TP
.BR \-\-images " " \fIMODE\fR
Inline images:
.BR auto " (default, detect the terminal), " never ,
.BR kitty " or " iterm2
(force a protocol).
Only local files are displayed; remote images are never downloaded.
.TP
.BR \-\-big\-headings " " \fIWHEN\fR
Scale headings by level with the Kitty text sizing protocol:
.BR auto " (default), " always " or " never .
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Color theme:
.BR ansi " (default, uses the terminal palette), " dark " or " light .
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use only ASCII symbols for list markers, quotes, rules and table borders.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set and not empty, disables colors (bold and italic remain).
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
If set and not 0, forces styled output even when standard output is not a
terminal.
.TP
.BR COLORTERM ", " TERM
Determine the color depth:
.B COLORTERM=truecolor
enables 24-bit color,
.B TERM=*256color*
256 colors, and
.B TERM=dumb
disables styling.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
A non-UTF-8 locale selects ASCII symbols.
.TP
.B INKMD_THEME
Default theme, as for
.BR \-\-theme .
.TP
.B INKMD_DEBUG
If set to 1, explains terminal capability detection and image decisions on
standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file could not be read; the others were still rendered.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line usage.
.SH SECURITY
Documents are treated as untrusted.
Control characters from the document are replaced by visible symbols, so a
document cannot send escape sequences to the terminal.
Nothing in a document is executed and nothing is downloaded.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B inkmd README.md
Render a file.
.TP
.B curl \-s https://example.com/doc.md | inkmd
Render Markdown from another program.
.TP
.B inkmd \-\-color always README.md | less \-R
Page a long document while keeping colors.
.TP
.B INKMD_DEBUG=1 inkmd doc.md
Show why images are or are not displayed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1)
.PP
https://github.com/alejandrofonsecacuza/Inkmd
